# How to cite this software.
#
# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this file.
#
# The list below is the citation author list, and its order is deliberate. It is
# not the contributor list: AUTHORS carries that one, reads it from the git
# history, and says why the two differ. `pyproject.toml`'s `authors` field
# repeats this list and has to be changed with it.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: "Erebots4.0"
abstract: >-
  A protocol-first framework for multi-agent conversational systems. A generalist
  orchestrator routes each request to a domain specialist, and agents are decoupled
  by the Agent2Agent (A2A) and Model Context Protocol (MCP) protocols rather than
  by Python imports.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aislab-hevs/erebots4.0"
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - large language models
  - agent2agent
  - model context protocol
  - conversational agents

